# NeuroVision — environment variable NAMES ONLY. Never put a real secret here.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored.
#
# Three different places read these, and mixing them up is the usual cause of a
# "works on my laptop" demo failure:
#
#   A. The Convex CLI on your machine   -> `.env.local` at the repo root
#   B. The browser (Vite)               -> `frontend/.env.local`, VITE_ prefix
#   C. The Convex SERVER (actions)      -> `npx convex env set NAME value`
#                                          NOT a file. See the note below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A. Convex CLI — written for you, do not hand-edit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `npx convex dev` writes these into .env.local when it configures a deployment.
# They identify WHICH deployment your CLI talks to.
# CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=
# CONVEX_URL=
# CONVEX_SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# B. Browser — must be prefixed VITE_ to reach client code
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Convex deployment the React app subscribes to. Same value as CONVEX_URL above
# for local dev. Public by design: it is only an address, not a credential.
VITE_CONVEX_URL=

# Base URL of Tom's FastAPI imaging service, e.g. http://localhost:8000.
# SPEC §6: the client calls this directly, there is no Vite proxy. Convex stores
# asset PATHS ("/jobs/sample/model.glb") and the frontend prefixes this.
VITE_API_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# C. Convex server-side secrets — NOT set in any file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Convex functions run on Convex's servers, so they cannot read your local
# .env.local. Server-side secrets are set on the deployment:
#
#     npx convex env set NEUROVISION_INGEST_SECRET <value>
#     npx convex env list
#
# and read inside a function with `process.env.NAME`. Listed here as
# DOCUMENTATION of which names the backend expects. Neither is used yet.
#
# Phase 5: shared secret the FastAPI service presents to the Convex HTTP ingest
# action before it may publish a job's status or results. Without this, anyone
# who finds the URL could mark a scan "completed".
# NEUROVISION_INGEST_SECRET=
#
# Phase 4: API key for the JARVIS summarisation LLM. BACKEND_CONTEXT §3 says the
# provider is NOT yet locked, so this name is a placeholder — do not hardwire a
# provider before the team confirms credits. The key must only ever be read
# inside a Convex `action`; chat and deterministic commands must keep working
# when it is absent (SPEC D8, BACKEND_CONTEXT §8).
# NEUROVISION_LLM_API_KEY=
